From 8b55d2c08045c5cc155236e3de5a35e346165a67 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Lothian <mike@fireburn.co.uk>
Date: Tue, 28 Jul 2026 21:20:52 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 102/106] drm/vino: add the encrypted control protocol

Add typed control-message encoding, AKE session handling, HDCP 2.2
transcript processing, and DisplayLink DL3 protocol constants.

Reuse DRM HDCP message identifiers and field lengths together
with the kernel AES, CMAC, SHA-256, HMAC, RSA akcipher, and random
interfaces. Keep session keys in memory-wiping Secret values and
reuse the configured receiver RSA transform for each downstream
authentication.

Validate counters, nonces, reply classes, and per-head authentication
state before encrypted setup can complete. Keep DisplayLink-specific
framing and key derivation local to the driver.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-0
Assisted-by: Codex:gpt-5
Signed-off-by: Mike Lothian <mike@fireburn.co.uk>
